      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does not seem we would need this anymore, so it can be removed. This is option is not toggled to True anywhere. No robot test set it to True and also jenkins jobs does not change this value to True.\n\nBased on response from Claude:\n\nThe toggle existed to let one shared test suite validate NETCONF device mounting against two different ODL connector implementations that coexisted for a while, rather than maintaining two near-duplicate suites:\n\nWhen True — the old config-subsystem connector. In early OpenDaylight (Helium/Lithium/Beryllium era), everything configurable in the controller — not just NETCONF — was wired up through a generic OSGi Config Admin-driven \"config-subsystem\": you\u0027d PUT a \u003cmodule\u003e entry describing service wiring (sal-netconf-connector type, binding-broker-osgi-registry, netty-event-executor, thread pools, etc. — exactly the boilerplate we saw in the default template). NETCONF devices mounted this way, oddly, showed up nested under a special controller-config node inside topology-netconf, because the config-subsystem itself was exposed as if it were a mountable NETCONF device.",
